<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought 54,000 tonnes of U.S. corn from Toepher at a tender on Friday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The corn was bought 87.80 U.S. cents over Chicago March futures, traders said.</p>
<p>Shipment was slated for January 26 to February 10 delivery from the U.S. Gulf or February 11-25 from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Members Feed Industry Group comprises Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
